### F19 — Dashboards (Tenant + Admin)
### Requer cookie "token" do usuario logado.
### Para o teste OWASP de admin, gere o cookie autenticando com um usuario nao-admin
### (sobrescreve {{token}}) ou substitua manualmente por outro cookie.

@host = {{base_url}}

### Dashboard Tenant — pagina completa
GET {{host}}/dashboard
Cookie: token={{token}}
Accept: text/html

> {%
    client.test("Dashboard tenant retorna 200", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, obtido " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.includes("dashboard-grid"), "HTML deve conter grid de blocos");
    });
%}

### Dashboard Tenant — fragmento HTMX (refresh manual)
GET {{host}}/dashboard/content
Cookie: token={{token}}
HX-Request: true
Accept: text/html

> {%
    client.test("Fragmento tenant retorna 200", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, obtido " + response.status);
        client.assert(!response.body.includes("<html>"), "fragmento nao deve trazer <html>");
    });
%}

### Dashboard Admin — pagina completa
GET {{host}}/admin/dashboard
Cookie: token={{token}}
Accept: text/html

> {%
    client.test("Dashboard admin retorna 200", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, obtido " + response.status);
    });
%}

### Dashboard Admin — fragmento HTMX
GET {{host}}/admin/dashboard/content
Cookie: token={{token}}
HX-Request: true
Accept: text/html

> {%
    client.test("Fragmento admin retorna 200", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, obtido " + response.status);
    });
%}

### ---- OWASP / erros esperados ----

### Sem cookie -> 401 (dashboard tenant)
GET {{host}}/dashboard
Accept: text/html

> {%
    client.test("Sem auth no /dashboard retorna 401", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 401, "esperado 401, obtido " + response.status);
    });
%}

### Sem cookie -> 401 (dashboard admin)
GET {{host}}/admin/dashboard
Accept: text/html

> {%
    client.test("Sem auth no /admin/dashboard retorna 401", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 401, "esperado 401, obtido " + response.status);
    });
%}

### Usuario comum no /admin/dashboard -> 403
### (autenticar com usuario nao-admin antes desta chamada para sobrescrever {{token}})
GET {{host}}/admin/dashboard
Cookie: token={{token}}
Accept: text/html

> {%
    client.test("User comum em /admin/dashboard retorna 403", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 403, "esperado 403, obtido " + response.status);
    });
%}

### SQLi em querystring -> 200 (parametros sao ignorados, sem erro)
GET {{host}}/dashboard?funnel=1%27%20OR%20%271%27%3D%271
Cookie: token={{token}}
Accept: text/html

> {%
    client.test("SQLi nao quebra o handler", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, obtido " + response.status);
    });
%}

### XSS em querystring -> 200, sem reflexao bruta no HTML
GET {{host}}/dashboard?x=%3Cscript%3Ealert(1)%3C/script%3E
Cookie: token={{token}}
Accept: text/html

> {%
    client.test("XSS nao reflete sem escape", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, obtido " + response.status);
        client.assert(!response.body.includes("<script>alert(1)</script>"), "payload XSS reflete sem escape");
    });
%}

### ============================================================
### F25 — Filtro de Dashboard por Usuario (Tenant)
### Requer cookie de um OWNER do tenant. Defina @operator_id com o id de um
### operador (nao-owner) do mesmo escritorio.
### ============================================================

@operator_id = COLOQUE_O_ID_DE_UM_OPERADOR_AQUI

### Owner: drill-down num operador -> 200 + indicador "Vendo dados de"
GET {{host}}/dashboard?user={{operator_id}}
Cookie: token={{token}}
Accept: text/html

> {%
    client.test("Drill-down do owner retorna 200", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, obtido " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.includes("Vendo dados de"), "deve indicar o operador filtrado");
    });
%}

### Owner: fragmento HTMX filtrado por operador -> 200
GET {{host}}/dashboard/content?user={{operator_id}}
Cookie: token={{token}}
HX-Request: true
Accept: text/html

> {%
    client.test("Fragmento filtrado retorna 200", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, obtido " + response.status);
        client.assert(!response.body.includes("<html>"), "fragmento nao deve trazer <html>");
    });
%}

### Owner: ?user inexistente/de outro tenant -> 200 consolidado (sem vazamento)
GET {{host}}/dashboard?user=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Cookie: token={{token}}
Accept: text/html

> {%
    client.test("Selecao invalida cai em consolidado", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, obtido " + response.status);
    });
%}

### OWASP: usuario comum (nao-owner) com ?user -> 200, mas escopo travado em si
### (autenticar com usuario COMUM para sobrescrever {{token}} antes desta chamada)
GET {{host}}/dashboard?user={{operator_id}}
Cookie: token={{token}}
Accept: text/html

> {%
    client.test("Nao-owner nao escala via ?user", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, obtido " + response.status);
    });
%}

### OWASP: SQLi no parametro ?user -> 200 (validado por pertencimento, query parametrizada)
GET {{host}}/dashboard?user=1%27%20OR%20%271%27%3D%271
Cookie: token={{token}}
Accept: text/html

> {%
    client.test("SQLi em ?user nao quebra o handler", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, obtido " + response.status);
    });
%}
